    'faq_json' => [
  ['question' => 'What is Senaei platform?', 'answer' => '<p>Senaei platform (industry.sa) is the official smart gateway for industrial investment in Saudi Arabia, affiliated with the Ministry of Industry and Mineral Resources. The Ministry was established by Royal Order A/472 on August 30, 2019 and began operations on January 1, 2020. The platform consolidates all digital services for industrial investors: licenses, exemptions, certificates of origin, labor approval, and integrations with MISA, Modon, and SIDF.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'What is the SADAD biller code for Senaei?', 'answer' => '<p>Payments to the Ministry of Industry and Mineral Resources are made through SADAD under the name "Ministry of Industry and Mineral Resources." The entity\'s programming code is 0029002000. When any invoice is issued for a specific service from within the platform (industrial licenses, certificates of origin), a sub-SADAD number is generated specific to the invoice itself.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'How much does an industrial license cost?', 'answer' => '<p>Initial license (establishment): free. Basic final license: SAR 2,000 + field inspection SAR 1,500. Annual renewal: SAR 1,200. Specialized industries may cost SAR 3,000-8,000 additional. Fees may vary based on activity, area, and industry. The customs exemption and industrial survey are free.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'What is the difference between the initial and final license?', 'answer' => '<p>The initial license (establishment) is a free document valid for one year, allowing completion of establishment procedures only (land allocation, factory construction, sub-license issuance) but does not allow actual production. The final license is issued after factory readiness and field inspection, enabling commercial production start and benefiting from customs exemptions.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'How long is the industrial license valid?', 'answer' => '<p>The industrial license is valid for one year, renewable annually for SAR 1,200. In special cases such as mineral exploration and exploitation licenses, the duration reaches 5 years. The initial license for establishment is also valid for one year to complete procedures.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'What is the customs exemption and how do I get it?', 'answer' => '<p>A free service from Senaei platform that enables industrial investors to obtain exemption from customs duties on: machinery and equipment, spare parts, raw materials, and semi-manufactured materials used in production. Basic requirement: obtaining the final industrial license. Application is submitted electronically from within the platform after linking it with Saudi Customs.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'What is the advantage of the SAR 100 work permit?', 'answer' => '<p>Exclusive competitive advantage: when a factory license is linked to Qiwa platform and labor approval is obtained from Senaei, work permit fees for expatriate workers drop to only SAR 100 (instead of the usual SAR 9,600). This is a major advantage for labor-intensive factories, saving thousands of riyals per worker annually.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'Can foreign investors use Senaei platform?', 'answer' => '<p>Yes, Senaei platform is open to foreign investors but with the condition of obtaining an investment license from the Ministry of Investment (MISA) first, then extracting the Saudi commercial registration. A Saudi national or Saudi resident authorized representative is also required to manage the platform account. Motaded Limited provides the integrated service from start to finish.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'How is expatriate labor approval done from Senaei?', 'answer' => '<p>An electronic service that enables industrial investors to obtain labor approval based on establishment needs. Procedures include: application submission via Senaei, field visit by the Ministry to assess workforce requirements, approval of the number, then extraction of work permits at SAR 100 per worker through Qiwa platform.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'What are certificates of origin?', 'answer' => '<p>Certificates issued from Senaei platform proving that the product was manufactured in Saudi Arabia, used for export to GCC and Arab countries to benefit from preferential treatment and customs exemptions. Two types: certificate with wet stamp at SAR 50 + VAT, and certificate with electronic stamp at SAR 75 + VAT. The electronic stamp is faster and easier for international accreditation.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'How does Senaei integrate with Modon and SIDF?', 'answer' => '<p>From within Senaei platform, direct applications can be submitted to linked entities: land/ready factory allocation request from Modon Authority (full partnership in Land and Loan and Factory and Loan programs), industrial loan request from the Saudi Industrial Development Fund SIDF, and electric power allocation request at preferential prices. This integration saves time and effort.</p>'],
  ['question' => 'How do I contact Senaei platform?', 'answer' => '<p>To contact: through Senaei platform industry.sa, the official Ministry website mim.gov.sa, or the Senaei mobile app (available on iOS). You can also contact Ministry of Industry and Mineral Resources service centers spread across the regions of the Kingdom.</p>'],
],
